# N4 (LMX_semantics.ru.md #activation-history; next_core_tasks_v3.md N4): the split call recurs over the same data
# and repeats. Each activation loads x from D, adds 1 and publishes before its inner call; after the inner one
# returns, the outer keeps its own working value (seen gets 2, then 1) and, clean, never writes it back. Entry 7.
int: seen 0
D:
    int: pad 4
    int: x 0
end: D
S:
    int: x
    x: x + 1
    if: x < 3
        call: S D
        node\seen: node\seen * 10 + x
end: S
fn: unit_seen () int
    return: node\seen
end: unit_seen
call: S D
int: first D\x
call: S D
int: r 81
if: first = 3 && D\x = 4 && D\pad = 4 && unit_seen() = 21
    r: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
